&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Analytical Thinking: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to diagnose complex technical issues within large-scale data environments and implement systemic solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attention to Detail: &lt;/strong&gt;A rigorous approach to data accuracy and the ability to identify subtle patterns or anomalies in high-volume datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven ability to work effectively with both technical engineering teams and non-technical product stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Skill in translating complex data quality issues into actionable insights and clear technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactivity: &lt;/strong&gt;A self-driven mindset focused on identifying potential risks and improving observability before issues impact the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications, Knowledge, and Job-Related Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Data Engineering, or a related technical field (or equivalent experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in data engineering, data quality, or analytics engineering, typically requiring 5+ years of relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL proficiency and expertise in managing and querying large, complex&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with data pipeline and orchestration tools (e.g., Airflow, dbt, Spark).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of data validation frameworks and automated testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working with high-volume, event-based data such as telemetry, logs, and user activity streams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within the gaming industry or similar high-concurrency, real-time data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of specialized data quality tools (e.g., Great Expectations, Monte Carlo).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with cloud platforms and data warehouses (e.g., AWS, Databricks, Snowflake).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with A/B testing frameworks and the nuances of experimentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of global data privacy regulations (e.g., GDPR, CCPA) and best practices for player data governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
