&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–6 years of experience in HR/People Operations, preferably in a multinational or technology organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with employee lifecycle processes and Workday HCM; exposure to UAT/testing is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of India employment practices and HR operations; exposure to APAC processes is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling employee transactions and resolving routine operational issues with appropriate guidance and escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to process improvement, HR systems, automation, or operational excellence initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to document processes clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused and comfortable working with employees, managers, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to take ownership of assigned processes, work independently within defined guidelines, and escalate matters appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to learn new processes, systems, and regional requirements in a fast-paced, global environment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important Note: This role requires working from our Pune office 3 days a week (hybrid work model)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
