&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own&lt;/strong&gt; the deal registration lifecycle for global partners, including deal eligibility validation, status monitoring, and escalation to ensure timely approvals, accurate CRM attribution, and program compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act&lt;/strong&gt; as the primary conduit between partner deal submitters, the alliance team, and field sales representatives to facilitate seamless communication, approvals, and conversion to Stage 2 qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize&lt;/strong&gt; the partner experience by reviewing existing registration processes to systematically identify bottlenecks, reduce errors, and drive operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transform&lt;/strong&gt; data into actionable insights by generating and analyzing deal registration reports to identify emerging trends and partner performance gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide&lt;/strong&gt; ad-hoc operational support for global partner initiatives, such as new partner onboarding and long-tail enablement and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage&lt;/strong&gt; day-to-day operations for the local team by setting priorities, mentoring staff, handling escalations, and ensuring deliverable completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assist&lt;/strong&gt; Global Alliances leadership with administrative activities, such as expense reports and calendar logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
