&lt;p&gt;Putnam are seeking an experienced strategy consultant with &lt;strong&gt;existing life sciences experience and, where possible, deep domain expertise&lt;/strong&gt;. Roles are &lt;strong&gt;practice-specific&lt;/strong&gt;, hired directly into defined Putnam practices to build sustained capability and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Consultant will be &lt;strong&gt;fully dedicated to the end-to-end project lifecycle&lt;/strong&gt;, providing continuity and hands-on delivery support to accelerate adoption within Putnam teams. This role is critical to providing &lt;strong&gt;deep domain expertise within their practice&lt;/strong&gt;, increasing value creation for clients and teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in teams to solve complex business problems for clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and analyze information, formulate and test hypotheses, and develop recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate findings and recommendations to client teams and senior stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation of recommendations and work with client teams to achieve impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively with colleagues across teams and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Requirements &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to solve complex problems and think creatively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and quantitative skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership skills and a strong sense of initiative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with people at all levels of an organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding record of academic achievement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple tasks and workstreams effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in a fast-paced, demanding, and ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional maturity, integrity, and a strong work ethic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in, or experience with, life sciences and healthcare markets (biopharma, medtech, diagnostics, or health services)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with topics such as product strategy, portfolio prioritisation, market access, commercial excellence, or growth strategy is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to rapidly build domain knowledge and apply strategy frameworks to highly technical client contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred qualifications include PharmD, MD/MBBS, PhD in lifesciences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant life science consulting or strategy experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on, execution-oriented approach with comfort working directly in data, analyses, and models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to commit to and support defined projects or practice portfolios over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideal candidate should be&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proactive, dedicated and enthusiastic, with a ‘can do’ attitude and approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate a high level of accuracy and attention to detail, as well as strengths in organisation and prioritisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a collaborative team player who works well with colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate ideas and issues in an effective, straightforward fashion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are highly motivated and want to seize opportunities to develop new skills and progress your career&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
