&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alteryx/UiPath Developer - BA Automation Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: 5-8 years&lt;br&gt;Location: Mumbai&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated &lt;strong&gt;Operations Automation Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; to work closely with Operations teams to identify manual, repetitive, inefficient, and risk-prone processes and convert them into scalable automation solutions. The role will use technologies such as &lt;strong&gt;Alteryx, UiPath, Power BI, Excel/VBA&lt;/strong&gt;, and other workflow automation platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will support the Operations transformation agenda by improving process efficiency, reducing manual touchpoints, strengthening controls, lowering operational risk, and contributing to departmental automation and capacity-saving objectives. Alteryx will primarily be used to automate complex, manual, Excel-based processes, while UiPath will be used to automate repetitive, rules-based activities to improve efficiency and productivity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have a strong analytical mindset, a practical understanding of Operations processes, and the ability to work independently with minimal supervision. They should be confident engaging directly with Operations subject-matter experts, identifying process pain points, translating business needs into automation solutions, and delivering production-ready outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Discovery and Opportunity Assessment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Operations teams to understand process pain points, manual activities, recurring issues, control gaps, and operational inefficiencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess processes for automation suitability, considering repeatability, data availability, transaction volumes, potential effort savings, risk reduction, and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate operational challenges into clearly defined automation use cases, business requirements, and measurable benefit cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support automation idea intake, benefit tracking, prioritisation, and delivery-readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation Development and Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, test, and implement automation solutions using Alteryx and UiPath, with potential integration across Excel, Outlook, Power BI, SharePoint, and other Operations tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Alteryx workflows to transform, reconcile, validate, and prepare operational data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop UiPath automations for repetitive, rules-based activities, including downloading files, navigating systems, extracting data, preparing reports, routing information, and reducing manual intervention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure solutions are robust, controlled, scalable, easy for Operations users to run, and straightforward to maintain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce runbooks, user guides, control documentation, and handover materials for business-as-usual teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Alteryx / Power BI knowledge including Alteryx Server / Power BI Cloud experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alteryx – Ability to develop complex workflows connecting to multiple data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Power BI – Being able to write DAX functions is a must to be considered advanced enough for the role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UiPath – Ability to develop bots using UiPath StudioX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills coupled with ability to support and upskill users in using the tool and building their solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data connectivity experience helpful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
