&lt;p&gt;Customers include Coca-Cola, Nestlé, Colgate-Palmolive, Mondelez, Samsung, and Kellogg&#39;s. Backed by SoftBank, Insight Partners, and Madrona. Headquartered in Mountain View with teams across the US, India, Canada, and the UK. Pre-IPO.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Security Engineer III to strengthen our cloud, application, and infrastructure security.&amp;nbsp;You will work closely with Engineering, DevOps, and IT teams to identify risks, implement security controls, automate security processes, and ensure compliance as we scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Cloud Security: Secure AWS and GCP environments, including IAM, network security, encryption, logging, and access controls.&lt;br&gt;• Application Security: Perform security reviews, vulnerability assessments, penetration testing coordination, and remediation tracking.&lt;br&gt;• DevSecOps: Integrate security scanning into CI/CD pipelines, including SAST, DAST, dependency scanning, container scanning, and IaC scanning.&lt;br&gt;• Infrastructure Security: Secure Kubernetes, Docker, Terraform, Linux systems, and cloud infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;• Security Monitoring: Improve threat detection, security logging, alerting, incident response, and investigation processes.&lt;br&gt;• Vulnerability Management: Identify, prioritize, and remediate vulnerabilities across applications, infrastructure, and dependencies.&lt;br&gt;• Compliance: Support SOC 2, ISO 27001, customer security assessments, audits, and evidence collection.&lt;br&gt;• Security Automation: Build scripts and tools to automate security checks, reporting, and remediation.&lt;br&gt;• Incident Response: Investigate security incidents, perform root-cause analysis, and implement preventive measures.&lt;br&gt;• Cross-functional Collaboration: Partner with Engineering, DevOps, IT, and Product teams to embed security into everyday workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• 6–10 years of experience in information security, cloud security, application security, or DevSecOps.&lt;br&gt;• Strong hands-on experience with AWS and/or GCP security.&lt;br&gt;• Good understanding of IAM, least-privilege access, secrets management, encryption, and network security.&lt;br&gt;• Experience integrating security tools into CI/CD pipelines.&lt;br&gt;• Familiarity with tools such as SonarQube, Snyk, Trivy, Checkov, Wiz, or equivalent.&lt;br&gt;• Working knowledge of Kubernetes, Docker, Terraform, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, or similar technologies.&lt;br&gt;• Knowledge of OWASP Top 10, common application vulnerabilities, and secure coding practices.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with vulnerability management, security incident response, and risk assessment.&lt;br&gt;• Scripting skills in Python, Bash, or similar languages.&lt;br&gt;• Understanding of SOC 2 or ISO 27001 requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status or any other category prohibited by applicable law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

