&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Commvault&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commvault (NASDAQ: CVLT) delivers continuous recovery for the AI era. We help organizations stay ready for constant disruption by returning critical data, applications, identities, and AI systems to a clean, trusted state. Our purpose-built recovery solutions span cloud-native and hybrid environments, leveraging AI to enable resilience at enterprise scale.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Data Engineer (Platform Engineering focus)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Platform Engineer designs, builds, automates, and operates the shared data and AI platform capabilities used by engineering, analytics, governance, and AI teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This senior hands-on role establishes reusable platform patterns across Databricks, Microsoft Azure, Microsoft Fabric, CI/CD, observability, security, and cost management. The role also provides technical leadership for platform reliability, operational maturity, and developer enablement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Architecture &amp;amp; Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement secure, scalable platform services for Databricks, Azure Data Lake, Microsoft Fabric, and supporting cloud services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reusable environment patterns for development, test, and production workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement workspace, network, identity, storage, compute, catalog, policy, and secrets-management configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Architecture and Security to translate enterprise standards into practical platform controls and reference implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation, DevOps &amp;amp; Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop infrastructure-as-code modules, deployment pipelines, automated configuration, and policy-as-code controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish CI/CD patterns for data pipelines, notebooks, libraries, semantic assets, and AI workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build self-service templates and paved-road capabilities that improve delivery consistency and reduce manual provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain source-control, release, artifact, environment-promotion, and rollback practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability, Observability &amp;amp; Cost Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement monitoring, alerting, logging, capacity, performance, availability, and recovery standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead troubleshooting and root-cause analysis for complex platform incidents and recurring reliability issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement operational dashboards, service-level indicators, runbooks, and on-call support patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze platform usage and cost drivers; implement guardrails, tagging, budgets, and optimization recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead platform design reviews and provide technical guidance to Platform Engineers and delivery teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop engineering standards, operating procedures, support models, and platform documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed data governance, lineage, classification, access control, and audit requirements into platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate platform features and emerging technologies, recommending pragmatic adoption paths aligned with business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in cloud platform engineering, DevOps, site reliability engineering, data platform engineering, or related roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience with Databricks and Microsoft Azure services, including networking, identity, storage, compute, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with infrastructure as code such as Terraform or Bicep and CI/CD platforms such as Azure DevOps or GitHub Actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing production-grade observability, incident response, backup, recovery, and operational support capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scripting and automation skills using Python, PowerShell, Bash, or comparable languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of lakehouse, data engineering, analytics, and AI workload patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex technical initiatives, mentor engineers, and influence standards without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Systems, or a related field; equivalent practical experience will be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Unity Catalog, Microsoft Purview, Microsoft Fabric, MLflow, or AI platform services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with policy-as-code, FinOps, container platforms, private networking, and enterprise identity integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud or Databricks certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting globally distributed, business-critical data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
