&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly skilled &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Security Architect&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the design and evaluation of secure software architectures across a diverse range of systems and applications. The ideal candidate will have deep expertise in security architecture review and threat modeling, with a strong understanding of modern software development practices and security best practices. Experience with automated tools for security architecture analysis and relevant security certifications is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct in-depth security architecture reviews across cloud, on-premises, and hybrid environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform threat modeling to identify potential security risks and define mitigation strategies early in the development of lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with development teams, DevOps, and product owners to design secure systems and guide secure software design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and implement automated tools to support architecture reviews and continuous security assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain security architecture documentation and reusable patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide expert guidance on security controls, design patterns, and industry best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development and improvement of internal security standards, frameworks, and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on emerging threats, vulnerabilities, and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in application or software security architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of threat modeling methodologies (e.g., STRIDE, PASTA, OCTAVE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience conducting security architecture reviews for complex systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with automated security architecture tools (e.g., IriusRisk, ThreatModeler, Microsoft Threat Modeling Tool, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in reviewing architecture GenAI solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of secure coding practices, software development lifecycle (SDLC), and DevSecOps integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills to collaborate with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as CSSLP, CISSP, SABSA, TOGAF, or GICSP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated environments (e.g., finance, healthcare, or critical infrastructure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP) and associated security architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Agile or CI/CD environments.&lt;/li&gt;
