&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About DevRev&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DevRev, we&#39;re building the future of work with &lt;em&gt;Computer&lt;/em&gt; – your AI teammate. Unlike traditional tools, &lt;em&gt;Computer&lt;/em&gt; unifies all your data sources, tools, and workflows into a single AI-ready platform, giving employees real-time insights, proactive suggestions, and powerful agentic actions. It extends your existing software with AI-native apps and agents that work alongside your teams and customers – updating workflows, coordinating across teams, and eliminating repetitive work. We call this Team Intelligence: human-AI collaboration that breaks down silos, brings people back together, and frees you to solve bigger problems. Backed by Khosla Ventures and Mayfield with $150M+ raised, DevRev is trusted by global companies across industries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At this level, you&#39;re no longer just contributing - you&#39;re driving. You own complex product areas, raise the quality of work around you, and operate with significant autonomy. You&#39;re producing judgment: making hard trade-offs, owning them, and explaining what you sacrificed and why. At DevRev, this means designing the communication layer of an AI-native platform - the surfaces where humans and Computer exchange meaning, where conversations carry consequence, and where the difference between a chatbot and a teammate lives in the details of interaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Messages is foundational infrastructure. Every product team at DevRev depends on the patterns you establish here. You&#39;ll define how conversations begin, evolve, interrupt, resume, and resolve - across threads, channels, real-time exchanges, and async flows. This isn&#39;t feature work; it&#39;s the connective tissue of the entire platform.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end design of messaging experiences across DevRev - from real-time conversation flows to asynchronous threads, notifications, and presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define interaction patterns for human-to-human, human-to-Computer, and Computer-initiated communication that feel native to each context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make hard trade-offs between information density, interruptibility, and conversational flow - and articulate what you sacrificed and why.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for progressive disclosure and graceful complexity: messages carry metadata, context, actions, and links to the knowledge graph without overwhelming the reader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with engineering on the technical constraints of real-time systems - latency, optimistic UI, delivery states, and platform adaptation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Arcade (our design system) at the pattern level - your messaging components become the reference implementation other teams build on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor L1-L3 designers with enough structure that they grow visibly; give feedback that demonstrably improves work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8 years of product design experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level proficiency with Figma and prototyping tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of conversational interfaces, messaging systems, or real-time collaboration products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own outcomes, not just outputs - you can point to a behaviour that changed or a metric that moved because of a decision you made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing interactions that handle real-world complexity: progressive disclosure, interruptibility, optimistic UI, error recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinking - you consider downstream consumers, systemic coherence, and long-term durability alongside immediate quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills; when you disagree with a product decision, you bring an alternative with evidence, not just an objection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re driven by design excellence and produce judgment others reference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don&#39;t optimize for comfort - you optimize for the user, even when that&#39;s the harder engineering path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You navigate ambiguity by reframing problems before opening Figma.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The people around you do better work because of the quality of your feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think at the system level: before finishing any component, you can name three other contexts it will appear in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How do we work? &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Whatever your role, our values describe what we ask of each other.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be a bridger&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Look beyond your own role. Ask questions, share context and help others get unstuck. That may mean bringing the right people together or picking up a problem that doesn’t necessarily fit neatly into your job description.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Care loudly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We want your perspective, not just your agreement. Speak up when something isn’t working or someone needs support. Give honest feedback with respect for the person receiving it. Don’t let an uncomfortable conversation become an unspoken problem.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the outcome&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Take responsibility for the result, not just your part in the process. Use AI to move the work forward, not to outsource your judgment. Make the call, check whether it worked and change course when it didn’t. If something goes wrong, own it and help fix it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;That’s DevRev!&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;DevRev is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition, or any other basis protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About DevRev&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DevRev, we&#39;re building the future of work with &lt;em&gt;Computer&lt;/em&gt; – your AI teammate. Unlike traditional tools, &lt;em&gt;Computer&lt;/em&gt; unifies all your data sources, tools, and workflows into a single AI-ready platform, giving employees real-time insights, proactive suggestions, and powerful agentic actions. It extends your existing software with AI-native apps and agents that work alongside your teams and customers – updating workflows, coordinating across teams, and eliminating repetitive work. We call this Team Intelligence: human-AI collaboration that breaks down silos, brings people back together, and frees you to solve bigger problems. Backed by Khosla Ventures and Mayfield with $150M+ raised, DevRev is trusted by global companies across industries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DevRev is hiring a Senior Product Manager for the&amp;nbsp;Computer Data and Analytics Platform&amp;nbsp;– a hands-on product leader who will own the trusted data foundation that makes Computer precise, useful, and safe across every experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Computer should not merely report on work. It should understand customer, product, and operational context; reason across it; and help people and agents take the right action. The Computer Data and Analytics Platform makes that possible through a unified, governed, low-latency data layer that turns data from DevRev and connected systems into durable context for humans, applications, analytics experiences, and AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will define how data is captured, modeled, governed, queried, and activated across DevRev. The platform will support operational reporting and embedded analytics, while also enabling grounded, context-rich agentic conversations in Computer – helping users ask questions, investigate work, receive trusted answers, and take safe actions in the flow of work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to build the foundation for an AI-native operating system – where customer context, product telemetry, structured records, events, and machine reasoning converge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the Computer Data and Analytics Platform vision and roadmap &lt;/strong&gt;- Define and scale the platform that transforms operational and product data into reliable, reusable context for analytics, dashboards, applications, APIs, workflows, and Computer. Set a clear strategy for data modeling, query experiences, data freshness, governance, and activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build trusted, AI agent-ready data foundations &lt;/strong&gt;- Own the product direction for a platform that preserves source-of-record fidelity while making data easy to discover, understand, and use. Shape the abstractions that let Computer and people work with data confidently – including lineage, permissions, access controls, quality signals, and semantic definitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the data lifecycle from capture to activation &lt;/strong&gt;- Guide the end-to-end path from source systems and event capture through change data capture, durable query representations, and governed serving layers. Ensure the platform supports real-time and historical workloads without forcing every experience to depend on a single data store or query engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable precise answers and safe actions with Computer&lt;/strong&gt; - Partner with the AI platform to make natural-language data experiences dependable. Drive capabilities that allow Computer to retrieve grounded context, generate useful analysis and visualizations, and execute approved actions through clear permissions, guardrails, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build high-performance, flexible query experiences&lt;/strong&gt; - Shape the experience for interactive analysis, embedded analytics, and developer workflows. Leverage in-process and local query technologies, including DuckDB where appropriate, to deliver responsive, secure experiences for applications, notebooks, and agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design for multiple personas and levels of abstraction - &lt;/strong&gt;Serve developers, data and product teams, support leaders, GTM teams, and operators. Provide opinionated defaults and ready-to-use experiences for common workflows, while preserving composability for technical users building applications, integrations, and custom data products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion a platform-grade developer experience&lt;/strong&gt; - Treat data as a core developer product. Prioritize intuitive APIs and SDKs, documentation, modular primitives, observability, extensibility, and a clear path from prototype to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive platform-wide interoperability&lt;/strong&gt; - Ensure the Computer Data and Analytics Platform works seamlessly with DevRev’s product data, customer records, connected systems, applications, workflows, and AI agents. Establish the shared data contracts and platform capabilities that power a complete customer and product understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;of product management or complementary experience building data platforms, developer platforms, analytics products, AI products, or infrastructure products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining products that span data ingestion, data modeling, data quality, governance, querying, and downstream activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern data architectures, including source systems, event streams, change data capture, lakehouse-style storage, query engines, and serving layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with embedded and in-process analytics, such as DuckDB, and the trade-offs between local, operational, and centralized query patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of AI-native data experiences, including grounded retrieval, natural-language querying, Text-to-SQL, evaluation, permissions, and safe action execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design products that serve both technical and non-technical users without compromising trust, usability, or extensibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of partnering deeply with engineering, design, AI/ML, security, and go-to-market teams to ship reliable, scalable platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment in ambiguous, technical environments – with the ability to turn an architectural direction into clear customer value, milestones, and adoption measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-file_viewer p-file_viewer--no_offset&quot; data-media-focus-container=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
