&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;DriveWealth is on a mission to make investing easier. We believe that everyone should have the ability to control their financial future, and that access to financial markets should not be limited by geography, wealth, or legacy systems. We are a global B2B financial technology organization dedicated to democratizing access to financial independence around the world. Our mission is realized through an API-based platform, empowering our partners to offer seamless investing and trading experiences to clients worldwide, all from their mobile devices. Our technology provides partners with a modern, extensible toolkit, enabling traditional investment workflows and innovative techniques like fractional share ownership. DriveWealth has evolved into a global platform offering trading of US equities, mutual funds, ETFs, fixed income, and options.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;There’s never been a better time to build a category-defining business and there has rarely been a team better positioned for this opportunity. Our culture blends the pace and agility of a fintech start-up with the impact, stability, and discipline of Wall Street. We encourage creativity and experimentation while ensuring institutional-grade execution and regulatory compliance in everything we do. Join us and help build the future of global investing!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The overnight Transaction Reporting Analyst is a critical role responsible for the operational integrity of DriveWealth&#39;s regulatory trade reporting during the newly extended 24/5 equity trading session. This role owns the overnight monitoring, exception handling, and repair of trade reporting submissions to FINRA&#39;s Trade Reporting Facility (TRF). The role also assists with other aspects of brokerage trade reporting, including the Consolidated Audit Trail (CAT) and Electronic Blue Sheets (EBS). This Transaction Reporting Analyst acts as the first line of defense against reporting breaks before the U.S. core trading day begins. This role works cross-functionally with Brokerage Operations, Compliance, and the U.S.-based Trade Reporting team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor TRF and ORF (Trade Reporting Facility) submissions overnight for health, rejections, and out-of-tolerance conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the 9:00pm (NYC Time) TRF opening rejection repair process, correcting and resubmitting failed trade reports within FINRA&#39;s reporting windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and manage the EBS (Electronic Blue Sheets) submission queue, escalating unresolved items to the U.S. team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm successful completion of CAT (Consolidated Audit Trail) submissions, investigating and escalating failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare detailed end-of-shift reports summarizing exceptions, open items, and notable activity for the incoming U.S. team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate unresolved or high-severity issues promptly, exercising judgment on when an issue requires immediate U.S. involvement versus next-business-day follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organized, auditable records of all monitoring activity, repairs, and escalations in line with the firm&#39;s written supervisory procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build working familiarity with FINRA/SEC trade reporting rules to identify patterns and recommend process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Brokerage Operations to improve the automation and reliability of overnight monitoring workflows.&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Minimum 2+ years of experience in financial services operations, trade support, or regulatory reporting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Direct exposure to FINRA trade reporting (TRF/CAT/EBS) or equivalent regulatory transaction reporting (e.g., MiFID II or EMIR transaction reporting) is a plus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Ability to work a shift aligned to the U.S. overnight trading session. Shift starts at 6:30 AM IST.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;A track record of ownership and disciplined execution in high-stakes, deadline-driven environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The ability to prioritize effectively and know when to escalate versus resolve independently.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Strong written communication skills — this role&#39;s primary deliverable to the U.S. team each day is a clear, accurate handoff report.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Impeccable integrity, sound judgment, high attention to detail and a deep respect for risk, controls, and regulatory obligations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (or local equivalent post-secondary qualification) in Finance, Business, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
