&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT EARNIN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As one of the first pioneers of earned wage access, our passion at EarnIn is building products that deliver real-time financial flexibility for people living paycheck to paycheck. Our community members access their earnings as they earn them, with options to spend, save, and grow their money without mandatory fees, interest rates, or credit checks.&amp;nbsp;We’re fortunate to have an incredibly experienced leadership team, combined with world-class funding partners like A16Z, Matrix Partners, DST, Ribbit Capital, and a very healthy core business with a tremendous runway. We’re growing fast and excited to bring on world-class talent to help shape the next chapter of our growth journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EarnIn is becoming an AI-native company, embedding AI agents into how we build, analyze, and operate across every function. Teams use AI Agents to move from ideas to execution faster. By letting agents handle repetitive tasks, our people can focus on judgment, creativity, and hard problems. We pair this experimentation with the strict review and security guardrails our regulated financial environment requires, always keeping a focus on privacy and the people who rely on our products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a company, we are becoming AI-native, and we encourage you to use AI tools throughout much of your interview process. If you use AI during the live interview, just say so; a quick, natural mention of how it helped and why you are using it is all we need. What we&#39;re evaluating is your judgment, reasoning, and ability to own and defend your work, not whether AI was involved. Some rounds, particularly those focused on your career history and past experiences, will not allow the use of AI, and we&#39;ll let you know of those in advance. When in doubt, ask your recruiter or interviewer directly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re looking for a highly creative and self-motivated Staff Product Designer to join EarnIn&#39;s Financial Intelligence Platform team. This is a structured, quality-focused group responsible for designing and improving the foundational experiences that power EarnIn&#39;s modern platform for financial flexibility and financial wellness for its community members. You&#39;ll work closely with product, engineering, design, compliance, risk, and finance partners to define and drive design excellence across core features like bank connectivity, earnings tracking, and repayment experiences. This role bridges deep design leadership with cross-functional execution, championing both customer and business value while ensuring quality, simplicity, and regulatory compliance. Your work will directly influence customer satisfaction and retention across our core experiences.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;This position will be a hybrid role based in our Bengaluru office, with 2 days on-site as part of our expanding site. EarnIn provides excellent benefits for our employees, including healthcare, internet/cell phone reimbursement, a learning and development stipend, and potential opportunities to travel to our Palo Alto HQ. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and refine core experiences across the full customer journey—from bank connection and account setup to earnings tracking and repayment experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with PMs, engineering, and data teams to define design requirements and validate solutions through research and usability testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain design patterns and systems that ensure consistency and simplicity across Financial Intelligence Platform features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify friction points in critical flows and design thoughtful solutions that improve usability, clarity, confidence, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage research findings and customer feedback to inform design strategy and prioritize improvements that deliver measurable impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion quality and polish, ensuring every interaction reflects EarnIn&#39;s commitment to reliability, trust, and regulatory standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Compliance, Risk, and Finance teams to ensure designs meet industry and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a culture of collaboration, continuous learning, and design excellence within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE&#39;RE LOOKING FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience designing consumer-facing digital products, with demonstrated success on core experiences or core functionality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio showcasing thoughtful problem-solving, systematic design, and measurable improvements to user satisfaction and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of financial products, user trust, and how to design for clarity in complex workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance creative thinking with research-driven validation, comfortable collaborating with data teams to measure impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent storytelling and communication skills, particularly in articulating design rationale to cross-functional stakeholders at all levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in Figma, prototyping tools, and modern design workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in structured environments where roadmaps are planned across product areas, with the ability to drive projects to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for solving real customer problems and improving financial wellness for everyday people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in systems design, design patterns, or design operations preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving user satisfaction and retention metrics through design-driven solutions is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At EarnIn, we believe that the best way to build a financial system that works for everyday people is by hiring a team that represents our diverse community. Our team is diverse not only in background and experience but also in perspective. We celebrate our diversity and strive to create a culture of belonging. EarnIn does not unlawfully discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, breastfeeding, or related medical conditions), gender identity, gender expression, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, legally protected medical condition, family care status, military or veteran status, marital status, registered domestic partner status, sexual orientation, genetic information, or any other basis protected by local, state, or federal laws. EarnIn is an E-Verify participant.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;EarnIn does not accept unsolicited resumes from individual recruiters or third-party recruiting agencies in response to job postings. No fee will be paid to third parties who submit unsolicited candidates directly to our hiring managers or HR team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;About Epic&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Kids is the leading digital reading platform built for kids 12 and under, trusted by millions of children, educators, and families around the world. Our mission is to inspire a lifelong love of reading by providing unlimited access to thousands of high-quality books, videos, and educational content through a safe and engaging experience. We combine technology, storytelling, and learning innovation to help every child become a confident reader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll join a collaborative and fast-paced global team passionate about building meaningful products that make a real impact on children&#39;s education and literacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own Epic&#39;s native Android app, the main way kids open a book on Android phones, tablets and Chromebooks. It&#39;s a large, mature Kotlin codebase with some Java and xml UI layouts. You&#39;ll work independently and partner closely with our Android, iOS, backend and web engineers and with the US engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own and evolve the Android app across phones, tablets and Chromebooks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the reading experience: our in-house page renderer and page-flip animation, zoom and gestures, and Read-to-Me audio synced to word highlighting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own offline reading (encrypted downloads, background work, local storage), Google Play Billing subscriptions, and the Play Store release pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive performance, stability and quality: startup time, memory, ANRs and crashes, and test coverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modernize carefully: move legacy Java and RxJava code forward without breaking a live app. also move to compose UIs whenever possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over time, pick up some iOS/Swift work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4 - 6 years of building and shipping native Android apps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong Kotlin, and comfortable working in mixed Kotlin and Java code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep experience with the Android View system, Fragments and custom Views: custom drawing, animation and touch handling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reactive and async programming: RxJava 2 in production, plus Kotlin coroutines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dependency injection, MVP or MVVM architecture and Networking with Retrofit and OkHttp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Local persistence with Room/SQLite, including schema migrations, and background work with WorkManager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Google Play Billing and the release pipeline: Gradle build variants, app signing, CI (Jenkins or similar), Play Console tracks and staged rollouts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testing with JUnit, Mockito or MockK, Robolectric and Espresso.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Media: ExoPlayer/Media3, MediaPlayer, and syncing audio to text.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Handling encrypted media and content stored offline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jetpack Compose, and the judgment to know when it fits alongside an existing View-based codebase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Performance tooling: Perfetto, Android Studio profilers, LeakCanary, New Relic or Crashlytics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with kids&#39; or education apps and children&#39;s privacy rules (COPPA).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interest in cross-platform mobile and some familiarity with iOS/Swift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40–50 LPA, with some flexibility for exceptional candidates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-section-id=&quot;16kvosu&quot; data-start=&quot;171&quot; data-end=&quot;182&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;184&quot; data-end=&quot;636&quot;&gt;Epic Kids is the leading digital reading platform built for kids 12 and under, trusted by millions of children, educators, and families around the world. Our mission is to inspire a lifelong love of reading by providing unlimited access to thousands of high-quality books, videos, and educational content through a safe and engaging experience. We combine technology, storytelling, and learning innovation to help every child become a confident reader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;638&quot; data-end=&quot;809&quot;&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll join a collaborative and fast-paced global team passionate about building meaningful products that make a real impact on children&#39;s education and literacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;1wct3r9&quot; data-start=&quot;811&quot; data-end=&quot;828&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;830&quot; data-end=&quot;1115&quot;&gt;The Senior iOS Engineer owns Epic&#39;s native iOS app -- the primary way our readers open a book on iPhone and iPad. You work independently on a large, established Swift and Objective-C codebase, own the reading experience end-to-end, and partner with our Android, backend, and web teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1117&quot; data-end=&quot;1222&quot;&gt;This is a role based in India, working closely with Epic&#39;s US engineering team and the wider global team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;11vcmyo&quot; data-start=&quot;1224&quot; data-end=&quot;1241&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1243&quot; data-end=&quot;1818&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;spjhue&quot; data-start=&quot;1243&quot; data-end=&quot;1359&quot;&gt;Own and evolve Epic&#39;s native iOS app across iPhone and iPad -- a large, established Swift and Objective-C codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1pkprab&quot; data-start=&quot;1360&quot; data-end=&quot;1485&quot;&gt;Own the reading experience -- the in-house book renderer and audio-text sync (narration aligned to word-level highlighting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1dho9q1&quot; data-start=&quot;1486&quot; data-end=&quot;1561&quot;&gt;Own offline reading, in-app purchases, and the App Store release pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1p804qb&quot; data-start=&quot;1562&quot; data-end=&quot;1615&quot;&gt;Drive the app&#39;s performance, stability, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1pjs7gh&quot; data-start=&quot;1616&quot; data-end=&quot;1703&quot;&gt;Partner with Epic&#39;s Android engineer and the backend and web teams on shared features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;dddekr&quot; data-start=&quot;1704&quot; data-end=&quot;1818&quot;&gt;Grow into a cross-platform mobile engineer over time, ramping into Android/Kotlin to contribute across both apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;nbk8dt&quot; data-start=&quot;1820&quot; data-end=&quot;1845&quot;&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;8b3p4d&quot; data-start=&quot;1847&quot; data-end=&quot;1874&quot;&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;1876&quot; data-end=&quot;2380&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1k5lfjz&quot; data-start=&quot;1876&quot; data-end=&quot;1941&quot;&gt;5+ years building and shipping native iOS apps to the App Store&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;kbykv7&quot; data-start=&quot;1942&quot; data-end=&quot;2033&quot;&gt;Strong Swift and UIKit, and comfort working across a mixed Swift and Objective-C codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;ip6n53&quot; data-start=&quot;2034&quot; data-end=&quot;2147&quot;&gt;Proven depth in custom UI/text rendering and/or real-time media-audio synchronization (not only stock controls)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;8r6xnv&quot; data-start=&quot;2148&quot; data-end=&quot;2325&quot;&gt;Solid across the iOS app lifecycle -- concurrency and thread-safety, local persistence, in-app purchase, and owning a release pipeline (CI, code signing, TestFlight/App Store)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;151n13c&quot; data-start=&quot;2326&quot; data-end=&quot;2380&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-section-id=&quot;19sla4h&quot; data-start=&quot;2382&quot; data-end=&quot;2402&quot;&gt;Preferred Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;2404&quot; data-end=&quot;2711&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;h35hhn&quot; data-start=&quot;2404&quot; data-end=&quot;2466&quot;&gt;Familiarity with SwiftUI and Swift Concurrency (async/await)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;17ha9od&quot; data-start=&quot;2467&quot; data-end=&quot;2515&quot;&gt;Familiarity with AVCadence for audio-text sync&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1r26309&quot; data-start=&quot;2516&quot; data-end=&quot;2558&quot;&gt;Experience with encrypted media playback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1yik6wr&quot; data-start=&quot;2559&quot; data-end=&quot;2638&quot;&gt;Accessibility on a consumer or kids&#39; product -- VoiceOver, Dynamic Type, WCAG&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;g31weq&quot; data-start=&quot;2639&quot; data-end=&quot;2711&quot;&gt;Interest in cross-platform mobile, and some Android / Kotlin awareness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;iwy669&quot; data-start=&quot;2713&quot; data-end=&quot;2730&quot;&gt;Why Join Epic?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2732&quot; data-end=&quot;3006&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to build products that inspire millions of kids to discover the joy of reading. You&#39;ll work alongside talented teammates across the globe, solve meaningful technical challenges, and help shape the future of digital learning for children.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Epic Kids is the leading digital reading platform built for kids 12 and under, trusted by millions of children, educators, and families around the world. Our mission is to inspire a lifelong love of reading by providing unlimited access to thousands of high-quality books, videos, and educational content through a safe and engaging experience. We combine technology, storytelling, and learning innovation to help every child become a confident reader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;At Epic, you&#39;ll join a collaborative and fast-paced global team passionate about building meaningful products that make a real impact on children&#39;s education and literacy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer, Full-Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;owns features end-to-end across Epic&#39;s web application -- Angular front-end, PHP/Symfony and Go services, MySQL -- and helps raise the engineering bar for the team. We hire for engineering strength over experience with any specific stack; strong engineers ramp quickly on ours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This is a fully remote,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;India&lt;/strong&gt;-based role, requiring close collaboration with a global engineering team that has members in the US, India and China.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship features end-to-end across the full stack, from spec to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound decisions on architecture, data modeling, and API design; document trade-offs and align stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive code quality through code review and testing across front-end and back-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior and mid-level engineers through code review and pairing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical design reviews, RFCs, and architecture discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-assisted development tools to accelerate delivery, holding generated code to the same quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in production support -- investigations, post-mortems, and systemic fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5 years of professional software engineering, owning complex, cross-team work autonomously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or higher in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong front-end engineering with a modern component framework (Angular a plus), plus solid TypeScript/JavaScript and UI fundamentals (HTML, CSS, accessibility).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong back-end engineering in a modern server-side language (we use PHP and Go).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relational-database proficiency -- data modeling, performant queries, and indexing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating production APIs (REST or gRPC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with Git, pull-request workflows, and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with our stack (Angular, PHP/Symfony, Go, MySQL) a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a service migration between languages/runtimes (e.g., PHP to Go) in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Tera for server-side templating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker and Kubernetes (GKE) at the application-developer level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud-platform experience -- GCP preferred, AWS or Azure acceptable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating against an observability stack (New Relic, Datadog, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of children&#39;s-privacy compliance frameworks (COPPA, FERPA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Eudia:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Eudia is redefining the future of legal work with AI-powered Augmented Intelligence, enabling Fortune 500 legal teams to move faster, manage risk more effectively, and unlock new business value. Backed by $105M in Series A funding led by General Catalyst, we’re building a category-defining platform that blends AI-driven automation with human expertise, transforming legal from a cost center into a strategic growth driver.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At Eudia, we move fast. Unlike traditional enterprise software, our teams ship solutions in days, not months—delivering real impact for some of the world’s largest companies, including Cargill, Coherent, DHL, and Duracell. We’re solving one of the most complex, unsolved challenges in AI: bringing trust, accuracy, and security to legal automation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We’re a team of builders, operators, and problem-solvers who are passionate about reshaping an industry that has long been resistant to change. If you’re looking for a place where you’ll be challenged, take ownership from day one, and work alongside some of the brightest minds in AI and legal —we’d love to meet you.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Are you excited about shaping the future of AI-driven legal solutions? We are looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Implementation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to help build next-generation platforms that power agentic AI models for the legal industry. This role offers the opportunity to work at the intersection of cutting-edge AI, scalable infrastructure, and legal innovation, building intelligent systems that streamline workflows, enhance legal research, and automate complex decision-making. It&#39;s a great opportunity to build enterprise-grade resilient platforms and services that are backed by cutting edge generative ai based solutions for some of the big Fortune 500 companies.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Good knowledge of scripting languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Quality &amp;amp; Best Practices&lt;/strong&gt;: Must exhibit high coding standards, conduct code reviews, and ensure adherence to best practices within the development team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Taking full ownership of significant modules and platforms ensuring its functional completeness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Working closely with other engineering teams, including engineers and GTM&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bachelor&#39;s in Computer Science&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Programming Skills: &lt;/strong&gt;Proficiency in multiple programming languages relevant to large-scale system development (e.g., Java, C++, Python, Go).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
