&lt;p&gt;Forward was founded in 2013 by four Stanford Ph.D.s, building the industry&#39;s first network digital twin: a mathematically accurate model of the production network. It&#39;s the foundation for autonomous networking, giving engineers and AI agents the ability to know the impact of every change before it touches production. That founding instinct still defines how we work. We&#39;re accurate and evidence-driven, relentless about clarity, and we&#39;d rather be certain than comfortable, building a groundbreaking platform that transforms how teams run and secure networks across every major cloud and vendor environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global leaders like Goldman Sachs, PayPal, S&amp;amp;P Global, IBM, and Dell trust Forward, alongside fast-growing enterprises and government agencies, realizing an average of $14.2 million in annual benefits, according to IDC. Backed by top-tier investors, including A. Capital, Andreessen Horowitz, Goldman Sachs, MSD Partners, Omega Venture Partners, Section 32, and Threshold Ventures, and headquartered in Santa Clara, we&#39;re most proud of our team: curious people who&#39;d rather build what doesn&#39;t exist than accept how things have always been done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forward Networks is currently seeking talented Network Engineers to work as part of our Network team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To do extensive testing of all the features available in routing protocols like BGP, MPLS, MP-BGP, RIP, EIGRP, OSPF, IS-IS, SR, etc., on multiple vendor platforms like Juniper, Cisco, Arista, PaloAlto, Fortinet, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach the basics of networking technologies and terminology to software developers working on creating models for those networking technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Requirements&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience operating large and complex networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Having strong knowledge of Service Provider, Enterprise Networking and Data Centre Technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the functionality of switches, routers, firewalls and load balancers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One or more of the following certificates: CCIE, JNCIE or VCDX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting or programming experience (Python, perl, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Ansible or other DevOps tools, git, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is a regular, full-time opportunity with Forward Networks in Bangalore, India.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Forward was founded in 2013 by four Stanford Ph.D.s, building the industry&#39;s first network digital twin: a mathematically accurate model of the production network. It&#39;s the foundation for autonomous networking, giving engineers and AI agents the ability to know the impact of every change before it touches production. That founding instinct still defines how we work. We&#39;re accurate and evidence-driven, relentless about clarity, and we&#39;d rather be certain than comfortable, building a groundbreaking platform that transforms how teams run and secure networks across every major cloud and vendor environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global leaders like Goldman Sachs, PayPal, S&amp;amp;P Global, IBM, and Dell trust Forward, alongside fast-growing enterprises and government agencies, realizing an average of $14.2 million in annual benefits, according to IDC. Backed by top-tier investors, including A. Capital, Andreessen Horowitz, Goldman Sachs, MSD Partners, Omega Venture Partners, Section 32, and Threshold Ventures, and headquartered in Santa Clara, we&#39;re most proud of our team: curious people who&#39;d rather build what doesn&#39;t exist than accept how things have always been done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forward is currently seeking a Senior Backend Software Engineer to work as part of our Platforms team. You will play a critical role in designing, developing, and scaling the core backend services and infrastructure that support our SaaS and on-prem deployments. Your contributions will have a direct impact on the stability, performance, and scalability of our platform, helping to ensure an exceptional experience for our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform development: &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute to the design and development of storage systems, job scheduling systems, data ingestion frameworks, monitoring frameworks etc to ensure high system performance and availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Feature development: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build and maintain backend frameworks that support essential platform features&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scalability &amp;amp; Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop scalable, high-performing, and reliable services optimized for handling complex workloads, and high-traffic loads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitoring &amp;amp; Visibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and improve monitoring and logging frameworks to provide deep visibility into system performance, reliability, and application health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with cross functional teams across our US and India offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read our blog to know more about the type of work we are doing:&lt;a href=&quot;https://forwardnetworks.com/scaling/&quot;&gt; https://forwardnetworks.com/scaling/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science or related degree; MS or PhD preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of full lifecycle software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Java (version 17 or later) and hands-on experience with Spring or other similar frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong object-oriented design and development skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with containerization and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of backend experience with Java, C++ or similar languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with REST APIs, as well as with frameworks such as Spring or Hibernate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Big Data and NoSQL experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE&lt;/strong&gt;: experience in the networking domain is NOT a requirement for this role but is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is a regular, full-time opportunity with Forward in Bangalore, India.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fospha.com/&quot;&gt;Fospha&lt;/a&gt; is dedicated to building the world&#39;s most powerful measurement solution for online retail. For over a decade, we&#39;ve helped teams make smarter decisions with full-funnel marketing insights, forecasting, and optimisation. With Fospha, every team moves faster and grows smarter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by &lt;strong&gt;leading brands&lt;/strong&gt; across three continents, including  &lt;strong&gt;Gymshark&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Huel and Oh Polly,&lt;/strong&gt; Fospha &lt;strong&gt;manages $4 billion&lt;/strong&gt; in annual ad spend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re scaling fast across &lt;strong&gt;London, Mumbai, and Austin&lt;/strong&gt; – and we&#39;re now looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join our Team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, you&#39;ll build the products our customers rely on every day to make multi-million&amp;nbsp;dollar media decisions. You&#39;ll work across the full stack - from crafting responsive, intuitive frontend&amp;nbsp;experiences through to designing and scaling the backend microservices that power them - and, given the&amp;nbsp;seniority of this role, you&#39;ll also help shape system design and infrastructure decisions as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside engineers, product managers, and AI agents as part of our AI-first operating model, where lean, high-autonomy teams ship fast and learn faster. This is a hands-on engineering role for someone who&#39;s comfortable owning a feature end-to-end - from initial design through to production - and who wants to grow their craft in a fast-moving, ambitious environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll focus&lt;br&gt;• &lt;/strong&gt;Frontend development using modern JavaScript frameworks (React.js or Next.js)&lt;br&gt;• Backend development using Python-based microservices&lt;br&gt;• System design and infrastructure, contributing to architectural decisions as we scale&lt;br&gt;• End-to-end feature ownership across the stack&lt;br&gt;• (Nice-to-have) Exposure to Data Science / Data Engineering workflows&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;• Design, build, and maintain full stack features - from frontend UI/UX through to backend services and&amp;nbsp;APIs in Python.&lt;br&gt;• Contribute to system design and infrastructure decisions, helping evolve our technical foundations as we&amp;nbsp;scale.&lt;br&gt;• Get involved across the full Software Development Lifecycle, from initial planning and design through&amp;nbsp;execution, release, and monitoring in production.&lt;br&gt;• Write clean, well-tested, maintainable code, and champion good engineering practices across the team.&lt;br&gt;• Collaborate closely with product managers, designers, and fellow engineers to translate requirements&amp;nbsp;into working software.&lt;br&gt;• Build and consume APIs (REST/GraphQL) that connect frontend experiences to backend services.&lt;br&gt;• Work with AI agents as part of our AI-first operating model, using clear specifications to shape high-&amp;nbsp;quality, AI-assisted engineering work.&lt;br&gt;• Take ownership of the quality, performance, and reliability of the features you ship.&lt;br&gt;• Participate in code reviews, giving and receiving candid, constructive feedback.&lt;br&gt;• Stay curious about new tools and technologies, including opportunities to explore Data Science / Data Engineering problems as they arise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What are we looking for? &amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Have around 5+ years of professional experience as a full stack / senior software engineer, with a balanced skill set across frontend, backend, and infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;• Have strong, hands-on experience with front-end technologies such as React.js or Next.js, and solid&amp;nbsp;backend experience building and maintaining Python-based microservices.&lt;br&gt;• Are comfortable contributing to system design and infrastructure decisions, reflecting the seniority of&amp;nbsp;this role.&lt;br&gt;• Are comfortable working across the full stack and can move fluidly between frontend, backend, and&amp;nbsp;infrastructure concerns.&lt;br&gt;• Have solid experience working in an agile environment and know how to embed quality into fast-moving&amp;nbsp;teams.&lt;br&gt;• Bring exceptional attention to detail and a genuine ownership mindset over what you build.&lt;br&gt;• Are enthusiastic about new technologies, with the ability to adapt and learn quickly - we&#39;re open to&amp;nbsp;candidates with strong experience in other modern languages/frameworks if the core skill set and&amp;nbsp;seniority are a strong match.&lt;br&gt;• Have an awareness of spec-driven AI development and how clear specifications shape the quality of AI-&amp;nbsp;assisted engineering work.&lt;br&gt;• Have the confidence and initiative to evolve ideas and pull pieces of work together into meaningful&amp;nbsp;change.&lt;br&gt;• Have an active interest in self-learning and growing your craft.&lt;br&gt;• Nice-to-have: exposure to Data Science / Data Engineering (not core to the role, but a strong plus).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t have to tick every box. If you&#39;re a strong engineer who&#39;s hungry to step up, we&#39;d still like to hear&lt;br&gt;from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Competitive salary&lt;br&gt;• Be part of a leading global venture builder, Blenheim Chalcot, and learn from the incredible talent in BC.&lt;br&gt;• Be exposed to the right mix of challenges and learning and development opportunities&lt;br&gt;• Flexible Benefits including Private Medical Subsidiaries, Life Assurance, Pension scheme etc&lt;br&gt;• 25 days of paid holiday + your birthday off!&lt;br&gt;• Quarterly team socials&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values and Principles - &lt;/strong&gt;You will be able to demonstrate examples of our core principles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Seek inclusion &amp;amp; diversity: We create an environment where everyone feels welcome, and people are encouraged to speak and be heard&lt;br&gt;• Work Hard, Work Well, Work Together: We take responsibility for making things happen, independently and together; we help colleagues in need and close loops, making sure our work is complete and has lasting impact&lt;br&gt;• Grow: We are proactive, curious and unafraid of failure&lt;br&gt;• Customer at the heart: We care about the customer, feel their pain and love building product that solves their biggest problems&lt;br&gt;• Candour with caring: We deliver candid feedback with kindness and receive it with gratitude&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Above all, our people show a willingness to work together and get their hands dirty to deliver product success, which means our customers are successful!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At FourKites we have the opportunity to tackle complex challenges with real-world impacts. Whether it&#39;s medical supplies from Cardinal Health or groceries for Walmart, the FourKites platform helps customers operate global supply chains that are efficient, agile and sustainable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Join a team of curious problem solvers that celebrates differences, leads with empathy and values inclusivity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Principal AI Architect, you will own the architecture underneath every FourKites AI agent: the harness they run in, the context they see, the models they call, and the evals that tell us whether they work. Our digital workers (Tracy for track and trace, Sam for supplier operations, Alan for appointment management, Cassie for customer service, Polly for document management, and more on the way) do real supply chain work on a shared platform, and you will set its direction. This is a hands-on individual contributor role based in Chennai (hybrid). You&#39;ll write code most weeks, lead design reviews across agent teams, and make the calls on model choice, context strategy and evaluation that every team builds on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the reference architecture for FourKites agents: the agent loop, tool execution, state and checkpointing, retries and recovery, guardrails, permissions, and human-in-the-loop handoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for long-running, multi-step work that spans many context windows and recovers cleanly when a tool, carrier API or model call fails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decide where each problem is best solved (frontier LLM, open-weight model, fine-tuned encoder, or plain code) and own model routing, cost-per-task and latency budgets across the fleet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate agents with FourKites&#39; event-driven platform (Kafka, microservices, Postgres) and with customer systems through APIs and MCP servers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the standard for what goes into an agent&#39;s context window (system prompts, tool definitions, retrieved documents, memory, prior turns) within an explicit token budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build shared components for retrieval, compaction and summarization, sub-agent isolation, prompt caching and persistent memory so teams stop reinventing them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose context failures (lost instructions, tool confusion, quality degradation as the window fills) and turn fixes into reusable harness patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the offline eval framework: golden datasets from production traces, code-based checks, LLM-as-judge graders calibrated against human labels, and CI regression suites that gate every prompt, model or tool change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build online evaluation: scoring sampled production traffic, trace- and task-level quality metrics, drift detection, shadow and A/B rollouts, user feedback signals, and quality alerts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect eval metrics to the business outcomes customers pay for, such as tracking accuracy, exceptions resolved without a human, and appointment fill rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review designs and PRs for agent teams, write the architecture docs and playbooks they follow, and mentor staff and senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track the model and tooling landscape, run the experiments that matter, and give leadership clear build, buy or wait recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Solutions and Customer Success to turn field failures into platform fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our product and engineering teams are dedicated to providing the industry&#39;s best-in-class end-to-end supply chain visibility platform. The agent platform sits underneath every FourKites digital worker, and the teams building on it ship agents that track freight, chase suppliers, book dock appointments, answer customer questions and read shipping documents in production. You&#39;ll be the senior technical authority for how FourKites builds, ships and measures agents, working closely with agent teams in Chennai and with colleagues in the US and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agents in production&lt;/strong&gt; : you&#39;ve architected and operated at least one LLM agent system with real users and real traffic (tool calling, multi-step workflows, failure handling, human escalation) and owned it after launch through incidents, cost and latency. Framework demos and POCs alone won&#39;t be a fit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep ML knowledge of encoders and transformers&lt;/strong&gt; : attention, positional encodings, encoder-only vs decoder-only vs encoder-decoder, tokenization and the KV cache. You&#39;ve trained or fine-tuned encoder models (BERT-family, sentence embeddings, bi-encoders, cross-encoder re-rankers) for classification, extraction or retrieval, and understand how contrastive training, distillation and quantization change cost and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context engineering&lt;/strong&gt; :you&#39;ve managed token budgets, built retrieval and memory for agents, used compaction and sub-agents to keep long tasks coherent, and measured how quality changes as the window fills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Harness engineering:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;you&#39;ve built the execution layer around a model: agent loop, tool dispatch, state and checkpoints, interruption and recovery, sandboxing and permissions, guardrails and model routing. Fluent with MCP, structured outputs and streaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on online and offline evals&lt;/strong&gt; : you&#39;ve built eval suites yourself: datasets, graders, LLM-as-judge calibration and CI regression gates offline; production scoring, trace sampling, drift monitoring, shadow deployments and feedback loops online. You&#39;ve used evals to block a release or justify a model switch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years building software or ML systems, with 3+ years building on LLMs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python:&amp;nbsp;strong, hands-on. Comfortable reading and reviewing Java or TypeScript services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience on AWS or GCP, containers and Kubernetes, and event-driven systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills: you can explain a trade-off to an engineer and its business impact to an executive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in supply chain, logistics or transportation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document AI: OCR, layout models, and extraction from bills of lading, invoices and PODs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Voice or email agents that act on behalf of a business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agent security: prompt injection defence, tool permissioning, and tenant data isolation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with several model families (Claude, GPT, Gemini, open-weight models) and serving stacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published work, talks or open-source contributions on agents, retrieval or evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;FourKites, the leader in AI-driven supply chain transformation for global enterprises and pioneer of real-time visibility, turns supply chain data into automated action. FourKites Intelligent Control TowerÂ® breaks down enterprise silos by creating a real-time digital twin of orders, shipments, inventory and assets. This comprehensive view, combined with AI-powered digital workers, enables companies to prevent disruptions, automate routine tasks and optimize performance across their supply chain. FourKites processes over 3.2 million supply chain events daily â€” from purchase orders to final delivery â€” helping 1,600-plus global brands prevent disruptions, make faster decisions and move from reactive tracking to proactive supply chain orchestration. For more information, visit www.fourkites.com.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FourKites provides competitive compensation with stock options, outstanding benefits and a collaborative culture for all employees around the globe. To help you be your best, we have 5 global recharge days, in addition to generous PTO and standard holidays. Parental leave for all parents, an annual wellness stipend and volunteer days also provide you with time and resources for self care and to care for others. Throughout the year, FourKites sets aside time during the workday to learn and celebrate diversity. We&#39;re always listening for new ways to support everyone in and out of the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical benefits start on first day of employment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;36 PTO days (Sick, Casual and Earned), 5 recharge days, 2 volunteer days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office set ups and Technology reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle &amp;amp; Family benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellness support and guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing learning &amp;amp; development opportunities (Professional development program, Toast Master club, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FourKites is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At FourKites we have the opportunity to tackle complex challenges with real-world impacts. Whether it&#39;s medical supplies from Cardinal Health or groceries for Walmart, the FourKites platform helps customers operate global supply chains that are efficient, agile and sustainable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Industry Context: AI-driven supply chain innovations reduce logistics costs by 15%+, inventory by 35%+, and improve service efficiency by 65%+. Companies prioritize AI-enabled automation as the key enabler for customer experience, sustainability, and resilience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Join a team of curious problem solvers that celebrates differences, leads with empathy and values inclusivity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FourKites is looking for a sharp, curious and execution-focused Product Manager to join the Visibility team and own our Over-the-Road (OTR) portfolio: Truckload, LTL, Parcel and Last Mile. This is FourKites&#39; flagship product line. Some of the world&#39;s largest shippers use it to track billions of dollars of freight every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a PM support role. You will own real product outcomes from day one. You&#39;ll work hands-on with data, build your own prototypes, talk directly with enterprise customers, and partner with engineering and design to ship features that improve adoption, retention and tracking quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role sits where supply chain operations meet modern software product development, and you&#39;ll need both. You need deep empathy for how freight actually moves across modes, and the analytical rigor to turn that into product bets worth making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Ownership &amp;amp; Outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product outcomes for one or more OTR modes (Truckload, LTL, Parcel or Last Mile), including tracking quality, ETA accuracy and carrier coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze adoption, engagement and retention KPIs for your area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find friction points and adoption gaps using usage data, customer interviews and feedback from Customer Success and Sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and prioritize a backlog that measurably improves customer stickiness, and bring well-reasoned prioritization recommendations to roadmap planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; AI-Assisted Product Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write your own SQL to explore feature usage, tracking performance and customer behavior, without waiting on an analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI coding tools (Claude, Cursor and similar) to build working prototypes, internal tools and quick analyses that make a requirement concrete before engineering picks it up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on in product analytics platforms like Pendo, and maintain dashboards that track adoption trends across customer segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn quantitative findings into clear product hypotheses and actionable backlog items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Data Science and Engineering on instrumentation and event tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run discovery sessions and join onboarding calls, QBRs and support escalations to understand shipper and carrier workflows firsthand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Customer Success Managers to surface systemic product gaps and recurring pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the customer in internal planning and sprint reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering and Design through scoping, development and post-launch monitoring, partnering directly with squads across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Product Marketing with onboarding materials, release notes and adoption playbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to presales conversations and market requirements gathering with Solutions teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring at two levels:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Associate Product Manager:&lt;/strong&gt; 2–4 years in product management or a related role. Strong BA, analyst, solutions or implementation backgrounds in logistics tech are welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Manager:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years, including end-to-end ownership of a product area and a track record of shipping with measurable business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For both levels:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience in supply chain or logistics. You understand shipper pain points, carrier dynamics and how freight moves day to day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working hands-on with data: strong SQL, familiarity with analytics tools, and the ability to build a data-driven story on your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven use of AI tools to speed up PM work beyond drafting documents, such as building prototypes, scripts and internal tools yourself. Be ready to walk us through something you&#39;ve built this way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer engagement skills. You&#39;ve run discovery calls, written user stories, and can turn qualitative feedback into crisp requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with distributed engineering teams across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with significant overlap with US Central Time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with two or more of truckload, LTL, parcel and last mile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work on SaaS onboarding flows, feature adoption programs or customer health scoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Pendo, Amplitude or similar product analytics tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with agile development and working directly with engineering squads.&lt;/li&gt;
