&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own delivery&lt;br&gt;• Own the end-to-end technical delivery of your team’s roadmap — from breaking down an epic into sequenced,&amp;nbsp;atomic units of work through to production release.&lt;br&gt;• Partner with the Product Manager and Engineering Manager to shape scope, sequence work realistically and say&amp;nbsp;no to the things that will not fit.&lt;br&gt;• Run sprint-level execution: identify risk early, surface and clear blockers, and keep commitments honest and&amp;nbsp;predictable.&lt;br&gt;• Be the single technical point of accountability when a release slips, a migration goes sideways or a customer&amp;nbsp;escalation lands on the team.&lt;br&gt;• Drive production health for your services — SLOs, on-call quality, alert hygiene, and root-cause follow-through&amp;nbsp;rather than repeat firefighting.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set technical direction&lt;br&gt;• Own the architecture of your domain: service boundaries, data models, event contracts and integration patterns,&amp;nbsp;aligned with the FourKites North Star architecture.&lt;br&gt;• Write and review design documents; make the calls that need making and document the trade-offs behind&amp;nbsp;them.&lt;br&gt;• Evaluate frameworks, tools and third-party/partner APIs; decide what we build, what we buy and what we&amp;nbsp;integrate.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain a live view of technical debt in your domain and negotiate a steady share of roadmap capacity to pay it&amp;nbsp;down.&lt;br&gt;• Design for the scale we actually run at — millions of supply chain events a day, across 80+ countries and 1,600+&amp;nbsp;global brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hold the engineering bar for the whole team&lt;br&gt;• Define and enforce the team’s engineering standards: coding conventions, test strategy and coverage&amp;nbsp;expectations, PR size and review turnaround, branching, observability and documentation.&lt;br&gt;• Review code with intent — catch design problems, not just style — and keep review latency low so the team&amp;nbsp;stays unblocked.&lt;br&gt;• Make quality measurable. Watch and improve the signals that matter: change failure rate, revert and hotfix rate,&amp;nbsp;escaped defects, MTTR, cycle time from first commit to production.&lt;br&gt;• Raise the floor, not just the ceiling: make sure best practices hold across every engineer on the team, including&amp;nbsp;the newest one.&lt;br&gt;• Champion secure-by-default and well-instrumented software — tests, tracing, metrics and alerts are part of&amp;nbsp;done, not a follow-up ticket.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Multiply the team&lt;br&gt;• Mentor engineers through design reviews, pairing and code review — technical growth, with career growth left&amp;nbsp;to the Engineering Manager.&lt;br&gt;• Give the EM and PM a clear, unvarnished read on the team’s technical capability and delivery risk.&lt;br&gt;• Onboard new engineers into the domain quickly, and keep the domain knowledge written down rather than&amp;nbsp;resident in one head.&lt;br&gt;• Participate in hiring as a technical interviewer and calibrate the bar for your domain.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work across the org&lt;br&gt;• Translate between engineering and the rest of the business — Product, Implementation, Customer Engineering,&amp;nbsp;Support and, when needed, the customer.&lt;br&gt;• Coordinate with tech leads in adjacent domains (OTR, Appointment Manager, Platform, AI Agents) on shared&amp;nbsp;contracts and cross-team dependencies.&lt;br&gt;• Represent your domain in architecture reviews and platform-level decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education Qualification: &lt;/strong&gt;Graduate from B.E/ B.Tech / MCA / M.Tech Background.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points: &lt;br&gt;For the Ocean Visibility&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Experience with ocean and multimodal logistics data — container and booking milestones, bills of lading, carrier&amp;nbsp;and NVOCC feeds, terminal and port data, AIS/vessel tracking, customs events.&lt;br&gt;• Familiarity with logistics integration standards and partner ecosystems (EDI/EDIFACT, X12, DCSA APIs, INTTRA,&amp;nbsp;CargoSmart, freight forwarder and carrier APIs).&lt;br&gt;• Experience reconciling messy, late, duplicated or conflicting third-party data into a single trustworthy source of&amp;nbsp;truth — and building the ETA and exception logic on top of it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For the Order Inventory Visibility role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Experience modelling orders, purchase orders, line items, SKUs and inventory positions — including order-to-&amp;nbsp;shipment and shipment-to-order stitching at high cardinality.&lt;br&gt;• Integration experience with enterprise systems of record: SAP, Oracle, other ERPs, OMS, WMS and TMS&amp;nbsp;platforms, over APIs, flat files and EDI.&lt;br&gt;• Experience building a real-time digital twin over order and inventory data, including OTIF, fill-rate and inventory-&amp;nbsp;in-motion analytics.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For both&lt;br&gt;• Prior work in supply chain, logistics or another high-volume B2B enterprise SaaS domain.&lt;br&gt;• Experience leading a large-scale migration, re-platforming or domain decomposition.&lt;br&gt;• Practical use of AI coding tools to raise team throughput without lowering the quality bar.&lt;br&gt;• Experience in a high-growth product organisation with enterprise customers.&lt;/p&gt;
