&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;About GenScript&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Founded in 2002 in New Jersey, GenScript Biotech Corporation accelerates innovation in biotech and healthcare by providing researchers and companies with the building blocks needed to develop groundbreaking treatments and products. Guided by its mission to Make People and Nature Healthier Through Biotechnology, and its role as a well-recognized biotechnology company, GenScript has a team of approximately 6,165 employees and has served more than 200,000 customers across over 100 countries and regions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Techno-Commercial Manager (Industrial Enzyme)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview &lt;/strong&gt;We are seeking a dynamic Techno-Commercial Manager (Industrial Enzyme) to join our expanding team in India. This remote role will focus on developing Technical Solution &amp;amp; On-site Support to ethanol customers and support sales head to enhance channel management to drive sales growth within the industrial enzyme sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;India, remote.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Activities:&lt;/strong&gt; Capable of effectively delivering technical trainings, facilitating in-depth discussions, leading and managing product trials and trial reports. Serve as the core technical and commercial contact for customers. Design tailored enzyme application solutions matching customers’ liquefaction, saccharification and fermentation processes. Conduct on-site process audits, parameter optimization and effect verification to improve ethanol yield and reduce plant energy and production costs. Resolve technical anomalies and product application issues quickly with internal technical and R&amp;amp;D support to ensure stable customer production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales &amp;amp; Channel Management: &lt;/strong&gt;execute grain processing industry growth strategies to expand market share by enhancing channel management and customer partnerships development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross Functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with technical and application research to drive product trials, problem-solving and support marketing in relevant branding activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Intelligence: &lt;/strong&gt;Identify trends, customer needs, and competitive positioning in industrial enzymes to contribute to business growth plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Background&lt;/strong&gt;: Proven track record in channel, key account management and B2B sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;: CRM excellence in managing opportunities pipeline, generating reports, forecasting, and ensuring data hygiene for cross functional team alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;: At least 5 years of experience in the ethanol industry. Prior exposure to enzymes is a significant added advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Technical Background&lt;/strong&gt;: Bachelor or Master’s degree; technical background (either through education or work experience) is preferred, with ability to bridge commercial and technical discussions with channels or customers and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultural Fit&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong teamwork spirit, ambitious mindset, and excellent communication skills. Experience working in multi-cultural environments is essential, with demonstrated leadership potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open to frequent travelling up to 50%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: &#39;Untitled Sans&#39;, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(45, 45, 45); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Benefits:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: &#39;Untitled Sans&#39;, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(45, 45, 45); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Benefits include medical, dental, and vision insurance as well as a 401(k) retirement plan with a company match that vests fully on day one. We offer paid parental leave after just three (3) months of employment, and a paid time off policy that includes vacation time, personal time, sick time, floating holidays, and company holidays. Additional benefits include flexible spending and health savings accounts, life and AD&amp;amp;D insurance, short- and long-term disability coverage, legal assistance, and supplemental plans such as pet, critical illness, accident, and hospital indemnity insurance. We also provide commuter benefits, well-being initiatives, and peer-to-peer recognition programs; demonstrating our ongoing commitment to building a culture where our people feel empowered, supported, and inspired to do their best work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 15px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: &#39;Untitled Sans&#39;, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(45, 45, 45); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;GenScript USA Inc/ProBio Inc. is a proud equal opportunity/affirmative action employer committed to attracting, retaining, and maximizing the performance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the Company&#39;s policy to ensure equal employment opportunity without discrimination or harassment based on race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, national origin, marital or domestic/civil partnership status, genetic information, citizenship status, uniformed service member or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: &#39;Untitled Sans&#39;, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(45, 45, 45); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;GenScript USA Inc./ProBio Inc. maintains a drug-free workplace.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: &#39;Untitled Sans&#39;, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px; line-height: inherit; font-family: &#39;Untitled Sans&#39;, sans-serif; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); letter-spacing: normal; text-align: start; word-spacing: 0px; white-space: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(45, 45, 45); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Please note: Genscript USA Inc./ProBio Inc. will only contact candidates through verified application sources. GenScript/Probio does not request personal information from candidates through individual email or any other platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Benefits Analyst on GitLab&#39;s Total Rewards team, you&#39;ll support global benefits administration and take ownership of day-to-day benefits operations in India, partnering closely with a Senior Benefits Analyst. Your initial priorities will include planning benefits events at the Bangalore hub, streamlining enrollment and benefits onboarding , handling tier 1 benefit questions and escalations, taking over and improving administrative and audit processes, along with routine benefits tasks.You&#39;ll build depth in global benefits and manage assigned work with increasing independence, seeking guidance on prioritization, new assignments, and higher-risk issues. This role reports to the Manager, Global Benefits and focuses on benefits programs, not leave administration. You&#39;ll need to be based in Bangalore, with periodic office presence for hosting and managing benefits events, and flexibility to collaborate across time zones, including Pacific time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support day-to-day administration for assigned benefits programs, including eligibility, enrollment, benefits onboarding, billing, reporting, audits, quality assurance, documentation, and issue resolution, with a particular focus on India.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review benefits and team-member data from multiple sources, research discrepancies and root causes, and recommend next steps for manager or senior team-member review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with brokers and vendors on day-to-day benefits operations, and support the Senior Benefits Analyst with renewals, plan changes, implementations, testing, launches, and post-launch improvements. Benefits plan decisions remain with the Senior Benefits Analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, host, and manage benefits events at the Bangalore hub, and coordinate assigned benefits activities across selected countries and employment arrangements. Apply documented processes and escalate questions that require deeper local or technical expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Payroll, Finance, People Operations, and People Technology on accurate reporting, billing reconciliation, eligibility data, and compliance-related processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support People Operations in resolving team-member benefits inquiries, explain moderately complex benefits topics in accessible language, and escalate cases appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze benefits utilization, cost, survey, and qualitative data to identify trends and prepare summaries, insights, and recommendations that support team priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate documentation, process guides, trackers, and communications; support the transition of administrative processes and recommend ways to simplify, standardize, or automate them, including responsible use of artificial intelligence tools. Protect accuracy and team-member experience, communicate progress and risks, and seek guidance on prioritizing improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting benefits administration, including enrollment, reporting, and audits, and working with benefits brokers or vendors. Experience supporting benefits in more than one country is required; global technology company experience is preferred. Strategic benefits plan design experience isn&#39;t required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of core benefits concepts, such as medical, dental, vision, life, disability, and supplemental benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using a human resources information system (HRIS), benefits administration platform, or similar operational tools, with attention to detail in data entry, testing, reconciliation, and quality assurance. Workday experience is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate or stronger Excel or Google Sheets skills, including VLOOKUPs, filters, pivot tables, and data analysis; macros aren&#39;t required. Ability to evaluate multiple sources, identify patterns or discrepancies, and develop evidence-based recommendations with appropriate guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain benefits topics in accessible language and collaborate across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage assigned work, meet deadlines, communicate when blocked, and distinguish urgent work from work that can be sequenced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, learning-oriented approach, willingness to apply feedback, and curiosity about using artificial intelligence tools responsibly to improve benefits work and team processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be based in Bangalore and go to our Bangalore hub to host and manage benefits events, with flexibility for collaboration across time zones, including Pacific time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Benefits team within Total Rewards supports global benefits programs, working with Payroll, Finance, People Operations, People Technology, Legal, People Business Partners, brokers, and vendors. You&#39;ll work closely with the Senior Benefits Analyst and colleagues in India, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Pacific time zones to support India&#39;s growing benefits needs. The team&#39;s tools include Workday, Google Workspace, Slack, and Claude. The role emphasizes accurate administration, team-member support, and practical process improvements, with opportunities to build deeper benefits expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
