&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is at the forefront of the artificial intelligence revolution, enabling innovators from all industries and sectors to expand human potential with technology. The availability of specialised artificial intelligence compute will be a decisive factor in AI’s rate of progress. Graphcore allows innovators to go further, faster. What we do really makes a difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced engineering leader to drive the design and development of complex, high-performance SoCs for next-generation AI acceleration platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines strong technical expertise with people leadership and engineering execution, requiring the ability to guide technical decisions, build high-performing teams and deliver high-quality silicon solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The SoC Design team is responsible for the RTL design, development and integration of critical subsystems within Graphcore’s AI acceleration platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works closely with architecture, verification, DFT and physical design teams throughout the silicon development lifecycle, from microarchitecture through implementation and sign-off.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership for microarchitecture, RTL design and SoC integration, driving design decisions and trade-offs across functionality, performance, power and area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering execution and delivery of complex SoC designs, ensuring alignment with project milestones, quality objectives and tapeout schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive design quality and implementation readiness, including CDC/RDC, synthesis, timing closure and physical implementation considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with architecture, verification, DFT and physical design teams to resolve complex technical challenges and ensure successful silicon delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and manage technical risks, resource requirements and cross-functional dependencies to ensure effective project execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and develop a high-performing engineering team through coaching, mentoring, performance management and talent development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement in design methodologies, engineering processes and team productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the design team in technical reviews, project planning and cross-functional discussions, ensuring alignment with broader engineering objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Electronic Engineering, Computer Science or a related discipline with 18+ Years of experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in ASIC/SoC design and development, including technical leadership and engineering management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading engineering teams through multiple complex SoC tapeouts, with end-to-end ownership of design execution and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in digital design, microarchitecture, RTL development and complex SoC integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of Verilog/SystemVerilog, SoC interconnect protocols and clock/reset architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of synthesis, static timing analysis, CDC/RDC, low-power design and physical implementation considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage technical risks, schedules, resources and cross-functional dependencies across complex silicon development programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in building, managing and developing high-performing engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgement, problem-solving and decision-making skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, stakeholder management and collaboration skills, with experience working across globally distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-performance, multicore or AI accelerator SoC development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with advanced process technologies and physically aware RTL design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of DFT methodologies, low-power design and multi-voltage domain integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-die or chiplet-based SoC architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of high-speed interfaces such as PCIe, DDR and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in silicon bring-up, post-silicon debugging and ECO implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience driving engineering methodology improvements and design automation&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is a globally recognised leader in Artificial Intelligence computing systems. The company designs advanced semiconductors and data centre hardware that provide the specialised processing power needed to drive AI innovation, while delivering the efficiency required to support its broader adoption. As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. We are opening a new AI Engineering Campus in Bengaluru, which will play a central role in Graphcore&#39;s work, building the future of AI computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Finance Manager – APAC will be responsible for overseeing the finance operations of Graphcore&#39;s APAC entities, initially India and Taiwan. Based in Bangalore, this role will provide financial leadership across the region while partnering closely with outsourced accounting providers, the UK Group Finance team and local business leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a broad, hands-on finance leadership role with responsibility for financial governance, statutory compliance, payroll oversight, treasury, business partnering and internal controls across the region. Whilst transactional accounting and local bookkeeping activities are performed by external service providers, the Senior Finance Manager retains ownership for the quality and integrity of the financial information, ensuring local accounting complies with Group policies and statutory requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will oversee monthly reporting from the outsourced accounting providers, manage the integration of local financial information into Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central for Group reporting, and support the continued development of scalable finance processes and controls as Graphcore expands across APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the VP Finance in the UK, this position will work closely with the wider Global Finance team, People, Facilities and local leadership to ensure Finance provides an outstanding service to the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance Operations &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the relationship with outsourced finance providers in India and Taiwan, ensuring agreed service levels are delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve monthly management accounts prepared by external accounting providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure local accounting complies with Group accounting policies and statutory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review balance sheet reconciliations and oversee resolution of accounting issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the finance lead for the APAC entities, ensuring robust governance and financial control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Group Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate monthly financial reporting from local accounting providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and post monthly journals into Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central to record the financial results of the APAC entities within the Group accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile local statutory accounts to Group reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support month-end close activities and Group reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support future integration of APAC entities into the Group ERP environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Statutory Compliance, Payroll &amp;amp; Treasury&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee statutory accounting, tax compliance and regulatory reporting across the APAC entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with external accountants, payroll providers, tax advisers and auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the People team, review and approve monthly payroll prepared by local payroll providers prior to processing.&lt;/li&gt;
