&lt;p&gt;Job Description&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Inizio,&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;we value inclusivity, recognize the power of diversity, and inspire the next generation of change-makers. We are an equal opportunities employer. We believe in creating a work environment that values diversity, equity, and inclusion. We strive to recruit from a diverse slate of candidates and foster an environment that provides the right conditions for long-term success. We welcome all applications regardless of race, colour, religion or belief, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, marital status, military veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation and physical or mental disability.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Contract Analyst is responsible for managing client contracts and building relationships both with our clients and across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is business partnering with one of our Business Units.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid working role reporting to a Commercial Affairs Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Business Partnering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster excellent relationships with internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides regular status updates.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contract Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with legal and agency teams to draft, review, and finalize contracts with clients in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures contracts meet quality and commercial standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages the contract lifecycle using the HighQ system ensuring contracts repository is kept up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports business and clients with contracting questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands key operational and financial drivers of allocated Business Unit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works simultaneously on multiple contracts and contract amendments&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Business Metrics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, manage and improve contract related metrics that demonstrate customer service.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relationship Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with clients and business partners to ensure customer satisfaction and foster long-term collaborations.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Problem Solving&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse information to solve problems and present proposed solutions to Management with Manager support.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communication and Negotiation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate strong communication and negotiation skills in engagements with internal teams and external clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively convey complex information and negotiate deals that align with the company&#39;s objectives.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What skills and experience you bring to the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keen eye for detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational, negotiation and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to solve problems, analyse information and achieve quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of contract language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and able to operate in a dynamic, fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of a bachelor’s level degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a commercial affairs / contracting role. Some background in working with Life Sciences / Pharmaceutical industry is preferable&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who are Inizio?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help our clients navigate their clinical development and commercialization journey by connecting the best scientific knowledge, market intelligence, actionable data, technology, communication, and creative execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a global presence and multiple career paths, the career possibilities are expanding at Inizio. We’re a growing global team of 11,700 - a $1.5bn revenue business working with the world’s leading health and life sciences businesses, and we have exciting growth plans. Whoever and wherever you are, we’ll empower you with the autonomy you need to experiment, learn, and grow. We’ll make sure that you feel valued, supported and, of course, because we’re helping our clients to transform healthcare and improve millions of lives you can feel pride in your work at Inizio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We invite you to come grow with us.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inizio Ignite is the global advisory partner for health and life sciences, bringing together connected expertise across Research Partnership, Putnam, Vynamic and STEM. Guided by purpose, passion and precision, we connect insight, strategy and execution to help clients make stronger decisions, accelerate performance and deliver lasting impact for patients. Data, technology and AI enhance this work, alongside the human expertise and judgement that define our advisory offer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the India Design Studio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are establishing an India Design Studio in Gurugram to support Inizio Ignite&#39;s global teams. The studio will operate as a central design hub, working with business-unit spokes across Research Partnership, Putnam, Vynamic, STEM and Innovation &amp;amp; Growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Design Studio will turn complex strategic, scientific and commercial content into clear, persuasive client stories. It will support high-value business development and client-facing work, including proposals, RFP responses, pitch decks, credentials, case studies, thought leadership and other priority materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to improve the quality, speed and consistency of these materials; strengthen how Ignite presents its connected expertise; and build reusable design assets and ways of working that support client delivery and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How quality works in the studio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quality is shared. Everyone who creates or edits work is accountable for the accuracy and quality of their contribution. Designers complete a structured self-check before handover. The Production &amp;amp; QA Assistant provides independent, checklist-based review and delivery control. The Senior Designer provides creative oversight and final design sign-off for priority or high-risk work. Business stakeholders remain accountable for factual content, client requirements and final business approval.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we use AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Approved AI and automation tools may be used to support brief understanding, content structuring, asset discovery, layout exploration, tagging and quality checks. They are enabling tools rather than substitutes for design craft. Human judgement, confidentiality, accessibility, brand integrity and final accountability always come first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your primary role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Designer - India Design Studio&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a developing presentation designer who delivers high-quality, client-facing work within agreed standards and timelines. You will improve the clarity, structure and visual impact of proposals, RFP responses, pitch decks and related materials, while building the judgement and independence required to progress in the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and redesign slides, proposal sections, RFP materials, credentials and case studies to improve clarity, visual hierarchy, structure and readability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Inizio Ignite brand standards, PowerPoint templates, visual systems and document standards consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate clear briefs and developed content into polished visual outputs, escalating gaps or ambiguity early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt existing materials for different audiences, clients, geographies and pursuit contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reusable slides, diagrams, icons and data visuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the design team and the Senior Designer on more complex visual storytelling and priority pursuits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the quality of your work, complete the studio self-check and resolve issues identified through design review or independent QA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clean, editable, accessible, well-named and version-controlled files that are ready for handover and reuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use approved AI tools responsibly where they improve understanding, exploration or efficiency, while applying independent design judgement to every output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to asset tagging, template improvement, knowledge capture and shared ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your skills and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Around 2-4 years of experience in presentation design, graphic design, visual design or a similar role, ideally supporting proposals, pitches, RFPs or other client-facing materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio that demonstrates strong layout, visual hierarchy, slide design, brand application and the ability to make complex content easier to understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong PowerPoint skills and working knowledge of Adobe Creative Cloud, Figma or comparable design tools; Think-cell or other charting experience would be useful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of typography, templates, design systems, iconography, data visualisation and document polish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication skills and the confidence to ask focused questions when briefs, priorities or source content are incomplete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and the ability to manage several workstreams within agreed service levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical AI literacy and the judgement to review, refine or reject AI-assisted suggestions before use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with healthcare, life sciences, consulting or professional-services content would be advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideal profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy turning rough or inconsistent content into clear, polished and client-ready materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can work confidently within templates while bringing creativity, clarity and visual thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You seek feedback, learn quickly and take increasing ownership as your skills develop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are collaborative, dependable and motivated to help build a new global design capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career progression&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within the Design Studio career framework of Production &amp;amp; QA Assistant, a Design team and Senior Designer. Progression to the next level is based on stronger independent ownership, visual storytelling, stakeholder management, delivery of more complex work and contribution to studio standards - not tenure alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Life at Inizio Ignite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a connected, global business where collaboration, curiosity, drive and agility shape how we work. We encourage people to bring their authentic selves, keep learning, challenge the status quo and do the right thing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the Design Studio, you will have the opportunity to help build a new capability, work with international teams and influence how Ignite presents its expertise to clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We provide&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A learning culture with opportunities to develop design, technology, AI and healthcare knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International collaboration across Research Partnership, Putnam, Vynamic, STEM and wider Inizio teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A supportive, inclusive and friendly working environment where your contribution matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A visible career framework, supported by regular feedback, skills development and opportunities to take on greater complexity and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Further information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time role and is expected to follow a hybrid working pattern, based at our Inizio location in Gurugram. The role will support global teams across time zones, so flexibility to work within agreed UK- and US-aligned collaboration windows may be required. The exact reporting line, working pattern and hours will be confirmed during the recruitment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Inizio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inizio is a global partner with over 10,500 experts operating in more than 50 countries. We support health and life science companies by turning science into strategy and executing across the product and patient journey. Our services include market research, strategy consulting, transformation consulting, and commercial benchmarking, all designed to be data-backed and patient-inspired.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking a highly detail-oriented and systems-focused Greenhouse ATS/ Talent Acquisition Systems Support Analyst to support the administration, maintenance, optimization, and reporting of our recruitment technology ecosystem, with a primary focus on Greenhouse ATS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role will serve as the first point of contact for recruitment system support, ensuring recruiters, hiring managers, and HR stakeholders have a seamless experience using our recruiting technologies. The successful candidate will be responsible for system configuration, user support, data integrity, troubleshooting, process documentation, and continuous improvement of recruitment systems and workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recruitment Systems Administration &amp;amp; Support&lt;br&gt;• Act as the primary support resource for Greenhouse ATS and related recruitment technologies (Linkedin Recruiter, HireEz, DataPeople etc)&lt;br&gt;• Maintain role-based permissions and user access across multiple business units and entities.&lt;br&gt;• Provide day-to-day support to recruiters, hiring managers, HR teams, and other system users.&lt;br&gt;• Support system testing, upgrades, releases, and implementation of new functionality.&lt;br&gt;• Create and maintain system documentation, user guides, and knowledge articles.&lt;br&gt;• Monitor system performance and identify opportunities for optimization and automation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Integration &amp;amp; Data Management&lt;br&gt;• Support integrations between Greenhouse, Workday, LinkedIn Recruiter, background screening providers, onboarding platforms, and other recruiting technologies.&lt;br&gt;• Monitor integration health and investigate data discrepancies between systems.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure data accuracy, consistency, and integrity across recruitment platforms.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Process &amp;amp; User Enablement&lt;br&gt;• Document recruitment system processes and standard operating procedures.&lt;br&gt;• Deliver system training and onboarding support for recruiters and hiring managers.&lt;br&gt;• Promote adoption of Greenhouse best practices and new system functionality.&lt;br&gt;• Partner with Talent Acquisition Operations, HR Operations, and HRIS teams to improve recruitment workflows and user experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;br&gt;• Experience administering or supporting Greenhouse ATS, Workday, or similar HR and recruitment systems.&lt;br&gt;• Strong understanding of recruitment processes and ATS workflows.&lt;br&gt;• Experience managing user permissions, templates, workflows, and system configurations.&lt;br&gt;• Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.&lt;br&gt;• Experience producing reports and working with recruitment data.&lt;br&gt;• High attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy.&lt;br&gt;• Excellent communication and customer service skills.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to manage multiple priorities and stakeholders effectively.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;br&gt;• Experience supporting Greenhouse integrations and implementation projects.&lt;br&gt;• Experience with LinkedIn Recruiter, background screening vendors (e.g., Sterling, HireRight), and onboarding systems.&lt;br&gt;• Advanced Excel skills and familiarity with Power BI, Tableau, or similar reporting tools.&lt;br&gt;• Experience supporting global recruitment operations.&lt;br&gt;• Understanding of data privacy and recruitment compliance requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
