&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Instawork is on a mission to create meaningful economic opportunities for skilled hourly professionals in communities around the globe. Our AI-powered labor marketplace helps local businesses scale, and enables global technology companies to push the frontiers of robotics and AI. Backed by world-class investors like Benchmark, Spark Capital, Craft Ventures, Greylock, Y Combinator, and others, we’re looking for exceptional talent to reimagine the way the world works.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Control Intern – Hardware&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Bengaluru, Karnataka, India&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Instawork is on a mission to create meaningful economic opportunities for skilled hourly professionals in communities around the globe. Our AI-powered labor marketplace helps local businesses scale, and enables global technology companies to push the frontiers of robotics and AI. Backed by world-class investors like Benchmark, Spark Capital, Craft Ventures, Greylock, Y Combinator, and others, we&#39;re looking for exceptional talent to reimagine the way the world works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;The Quality Control Intern – Hardware is the checkpoint every recording rig passes through, in both directions. When rigs return from the field, you inspect their condition, run a functional check, and capture a short test recording that you review to confirm the cameras, footage, audio, and storage are all working. Before any rig goes back out, you give the final sign-off that it is field-ready.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;This is a small role with an outsized impact: a rig that leaves your desk in a bad state means a Field Officer travels to a business, records for hours, and returns with unusable or missing data — a full day lost, and sometimes a burned business relationship. Your job is to make sure that never happens. Precision, consistency, and discipline are the whole game here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Nothing goes to field without your approval; nothing comes back without your inspection and log.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;You are the last line of defense on rig quality before it reaches a business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Inbound Inspection (rigs returning from cities)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Receive rigs and accessories (cameras, SD cards, card readers, cables, mounts) as they return from the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Check physical condition — damage, loose mounts, worn cables, cleanliness — and log it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Verify all issued components are present against the checkout record; flag anything missing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Functional QC &amp;amp; Test Recording&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Power up each rig and confirm cameras open, storage is available, and the device is charged/charging correctly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Capture a short test recording and review it: cameras correctly aligned, footage clear and stable, audio present, timestamps correct&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Confirm the SD card reads correctly, the previous session&#39;s data has been offloaded, and the card is cleared and ready for reuse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Only mark a rig &quot;field-ready&quot; once every check passes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Outbound Approval (clearing rigs for field)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Give the final go/no-go before a rig is handed to a Field Officer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Ensure the rig leaves fully charged, correctly configured, and with the right accessories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Sign off in the tracker so every field-ready rig is traceable to your check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Fault Handling &amp;amp; Escalation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Quarantine any rig that fails QC so it cannot accidentally go to field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Log the exact fault clearly (which component, what&#39;s wrong) and escalate hardware faults to the Hardware/IT team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Follow up so repaired rigs are re-checked before they re-enter circulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Documentation &amp;amp; Discipline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Maintain clean, complete QC records in Google Sheets — every rig, every check, pass/fail, date/time, and reason&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Keep the QC and quarantine areas organized and controlled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Follow the QC checklist exactly, every single time — no shortcuts, no assumptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Mandatory&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Some technical or hardware familiarity — comfortable handling phones/cameras, SD cards, cables, and basic device settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Basic computer knowledge; comfortable with Google Sheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;High attention to detail and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Discipline to follow a checklist the same way every time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Preferred&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Exposure to device QC, hardware testing, electronics, or camera/AV equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Experience handling or tracking physical inventory/assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal Qualities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;Meticulous and detail-obsessed — catches the small thing others miss&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Reliable and consistent under repetitive, high-volume work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Honest — never marks something &quot;passed&quot; without actually checking it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;Organized, disciplined, and comfortable in a fast-paced on-site environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Scale &amp;amp; Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li4&quot;&gt;On-site at the inventory hub, shift-based (6 PM to 3 AM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li7&quot;&gt;Reports to the Inventory Manager; escalates hardware faults to the Hardware/IT team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li5&quot;&gt;High-responsibility, hands-on QC role — critical to keeping usable field hours high&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;Our Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Empathy, Trust &amp;amp; Candor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We put ourselves in the shoes of our colleagues and customers and don’t shy away from uncomfortable conversations, instead building trust through honest and direct feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Bias for Action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We practice high-velocity decision-making, clear-eyed that we often operate with incomplete information. Growing quickly means it’s OK to be wrong, so long as we learn from our mistakes and course correct!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Always Be Learning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We’re a curious bunch, and with AI transforming our workplace we encourage everyone to learn from each other, compounding our knowledge and experience to help us change an entire industry.&lt;/p&gt;
