&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Instead&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Instead is where tax work gets done. Our AI agent orchestrates the entirety of how work gets done in tax, from preparation and compliance to filing and advisory. It’s a fundamentally new way of doing tax work, and it’s why top 500 firms, Big Four teams, and enterprise corporate tax departments are choosing Instead.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;What makes us unique: we hold full government approvals with the IRS, 48 states, and all cities to e-file 1040, 1041, 1120, 1120S, and 1065, with 706, 709, 990, 5500, and 2290 coming for tax year 2026. No one else can offer this, and no one else will for years as it takes that long to pass government approvals. This lets us build product experiences that are simply unmatched in the market.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Instead is backed by Conviction, IRIS (the largest tax software provider in the UK), Skylark, and many of our partners and customers. Our team includes leaders from Intuit, Thomson Reuters, Wolters Kluwer, Gusto, PwC, BDO, RSM, and KPMG.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The national publication Accounting Today, twice recognized me as one of the “Top 100 Most Influential People in the Accounting Profession - Ones To Watch”.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking an experienced Director of Talent Acquisition to lead and scale our global recruiting function at Instead. You’ll be responsible for overseeing the entire end-to-end recruiting process—from workforce planning and sourcing strategy through to offer acceptance and onboarding—across all departments and regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role leads a growing talent team, currently including two junior recruiters, and will be directly responsible for ensuring we attract, assess, and hire exceptional talent for every position across the organization. You’ll partner closely with executive leadership and department heads in the US and India to build scalable recruiting systems, deliver an outstanding candidate experience, and ensure our hiring goals align with Instead’s rapid growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, leadership role based in our Bangalore office, working closely with both India and US teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, manage, and mentor a growing team of recruiters responsible for full-cycle hiring across all departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute a global talent acquisition strategy that supports current and future hiring needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end recruiting process—including sourcing, interviewing, selection, offers, and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers and executives to define role requirements, success profiles, and hiring plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement data-driven recruiting processes, ensuring clear metrics on time-to-fill, pipeline health, and quality of hire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a robust candidate pipeline through proactive sourcing, networking, and partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee ATS management, recruiting operations, and compliance with global hiring policies and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a world-class candidate experience, ensuring professionalism, transparency, and consistency at every stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive employer branding initiatives to strengthen Instead’s reputation as a destination for top global talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve interview processes, scorecards, and recruiter enablement through training and tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in talent acquisition or recruiting leadership, preferably in a technology, SaaS or Tax services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing and developing recruiters and building scalable hiring processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of end-to-end recruiting across multiple disciplines (engineering, product, tax, marketing, G&amp;amp;A).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to partner with senior leadership and hiring managers globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern recruiting platforms, sourcing tools, and applicant tracking systems (ATS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and communication skills with strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a fast-paced, high-growth environment while maintaining quality and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building recruiting operations in a startup or high-growth global company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI or tech recruiting and global hiring strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience scaling teams across India and the US.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in employer branding and recruiting analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
